# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Frontend environment (Vite). Copy to frontend/.env (or .env.local).
#
# Vite reads env files from this directory only - variables in the repository
# root .env never reach the browser bundle. All of these are optional.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Data source -------------------------------------------------------------
# VITE_FIXTURES=1 serves every response from src/fixtures instead of the API, so
# the dashboard runs with no backend at all.
#VITE_FIXTURES=1

# Where the API lives, as the browser sees it. Defaults to /api, which the Vite
# dev server proxies to http://localhost:8000 (vite.config.ts) and nginx proxies
# in the Docker deployment.
#VITE_API_BASE=/api

# Where the dev server's /api proxy forwards to (vite.config.ts). Only used by
# `npm run dev`, never by a production build.
#VITE_API_URL=http://localhost:8000

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Base map tiles (frontend, build-time)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The map shipped with a CARTO URL hardcoded in the page. That URL still works
# as a request; what changed is CARTO's side of it - their keyless endpoint now
# returns watermark tiles reading "API key required". Nothing in this repository
# broke, and reacting to it took a code change. Now it takes an edit here.
# See DECISIONS.md D-007.
#
# All four are optional. Left unset, the map uses OpenStreetMap's standard
# tiles, which need no key.
#
# VITE_TILE_URL may contain a key as a query parameter, so moving to a keyed
# provider later is only a change to this file. Two examples, for later:
#   VITE_TILE_URL=https://api.maptiler.com/maps/streets-v2/{z}/{x}/{y}.png?key=YOUR_KEY
#   VITE_TILE_URL=https://tile.thunderforest.com/atlas/{z}/{x}/{y}.png?apikey=YOUR_KEY
#
# If you set VITE_TILE_URL, set VITE_TILE_ATTRIBUTION too: the OpenStreetMap
# credit is only correct for OpenStreetMap tiles, and crediting the wrong
# people is worse than crediting nobody.
#VITE_TILE_URL=https://tile.openstreetmap.org/{z}/{x}/{y}.png
#VITE_TILE_ATTRIBUTION=&copy; OpenStreetMap contributors
#VITE_TILE_MAX_ZOOM=19
# Only used when the URL contains the {s} subdomain placeholder. Modern
# providers do not use it; passing it otherwise makes Leaflet warn per tile.
#VITE_TILE_SUBDOMAINS=abc
